    "why": "Optical fiber must carry the 5.03B revenue bar while display glass absorbs October's panel cuts \u2014 proof AI demand, not displays, now sets earnings."
  },
  "reasons": [
    "The 8.1% fall to 123.99 was a JPMorgan target cut to $165 on valuation, not demand, because Verizon's 80-million-mile fiber order through 2032 already commits volume the Q3 print will bill.",
    "Because Optical Communications is 44% of sales, October's panel cuts hit the smaller Display segment, so Q2 revenue still rose 8.7% sequentially and 16.6% year over year, operating income up 21.8%.",
    "The Springboard plan needs a $20B annualized run rate by end-2026, about 5B a quarter, so the 5.03B Q3 consensus is the plan being executed, not a stretch above it."
  ],
  "watch": [
    "Optical Communications share of sales: holding near 44% confirms Verizon and AI fiber volume is converting; a lower share means the backlog is not shipping.",
    "Gross margin: Q2 was 36% (1.63B on 4.5B sales); holding near that confirms fiber pricing, compression means panel cuts are already biting.",
    "Revenue against the 5.03B consensus: at or above keeps the $20B end-2026 path alive; a miss breaks the Springboard math.",
    "Q4 guidance: at or above a 5B quarterly rate confirms the end-2026 target; below it, the $20B plan slips a year."
  ],
